WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.597
Identify, explain and apply the important ideas behind why we use databases.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:12.003
Database: is an organised collection of related information. Record: is one complete

00:00:12.003 --> 00:00:12.466
entry.

00:00:13.283 --> 00:00:19.440
Field: is a named piece of data in an entry. Table: arranges records in rows and

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:23.673
fields in columns. Query: asks a database to find matching information.

00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:29.440
Collect a few harmless facts about classroom materials, NOT personal details. Make a

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.347
paper chart with the terms Database, Record and Field; explain what each means.
